    <GaugingStation location="Bessom Bridge" name="Withiel Florey Stream" number="45818">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Broad crested flat V weir opened in 1992.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Well-built station and good control. Bypassing and weed growth are not an issue, but some drowning. Potential for blockage of culverts under footbridge downstream during high flows which may affect levels and drown out weir. One rating applied across period of record. Confirmed by gaugings to 0.6m, above which available gaugings fit poorly to rating and indicate overestimation of flows.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Station opened in 1992 as a broad crested Flat V weir, crest length approximately 4m. Relatively straight reach with stable river bed. Footbridge approx.12m downstream of the station. Velocity area station for higher flows.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2022 (WINFAP Files v11).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Fish farm upstream causes fluctuations in low flows.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Small catchment area consists mainly of Upper Devonian siltstones and slates. Entirely rural catchment area with natural flow regime. Wimbleball Reservoir downstream of the station. No major catchment changes.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff"/>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged above QMED. Good fit to gauging." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Few high flow gaugings which fit poorly to rating beyond QMED. Increasing uncertainty in rating beyond 0.6m." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
